      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Headache is one of the commonest neurological symptoms. One must first identify patients with structural disease requiring specific therapy, though this is unusual, especially in outpatient practice. While migraine, tension headache, and cluster headache are not life-threatening, they are major causes of morbidity, and much can be done to alleviate them."},
